  "thumbnailAlt": "Safety Training Quiz form beside a photo of male and female construction workers discussing plans at a building site",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A safety training quiz is a form that tests workers on hazards, safe procedures and emergency steps after training, so employers can confirm understanding and keep a record for each person. This template covers ten core topics, from the PASS fire extinguisher method to lockout/tagout, and grades every answer automatically against an 80% pass mark.",
    "audience": "Safety officers, HR and training coordinators, site supervisors and operations managers in warehouses, manufacturing, construction and offices.",
    "useCases": [
      "A knowledge check at the end of new-hire safety induction",
      "Annual refresher training for existing staff",
      "Toolbox talk follow-ups on a construction site",
      "Checking contractors understand site rules before starting work"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Quiz mode shows each worker their score instantly; set the pass mark to match your policy and ask anyone below it to retake after a refresher.",
      "Turn on 'require sign-in' and 'one response per person' so each result is tied to one named worker for your training records.",
      "Use the PDF templates feature to generate a completion record per response, and export results to Excel for audits."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a safety training quiz include?",
        "answer": "Questions on the hazards your workers actually face: fire and evacuation, PPE, manual handling, ladders and working at height, chemicals and Safety Data Sheets, lockout/tagout, housekeeping and how to report incidents and near misses, plus the worker's name, ID, site and training date."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does a safety quiz count as OSHA training documentation?",
        "answer": "A quiz can be part of your records, showing the worker was trained and understood it, but it does not replace the training itself or any specific documentation a standard requires. Check the rules that apply to your industry and country."
      },
      {
        "question": "What pass mark should a safety quiz use?",
        "answer": "Many employers use 80% or higher for safety topics, and some require 100% on critical questions like lockout/tagout. Whatever you choose, have a clear retake process."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I add questions specific to my site?",
        "answer": "Yes, and you should. Copy the template and add questions on your own hazards, emergency exits, assembly points and equipment, each with its correct answer set."
      }
    ]
  },
